  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Refugees and Host Communities Response in Gambella National Regional State</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam has been designated by United Nations High Commission for Refugees (UNHCR) to take the lead role of delivering full -fledged of WASH (Water, Sanitation and Hygiene) assistance to enhance the South Sudanese refugees hosted in Punyido, Punyido II, Tierkidi , Kule ,Ngunyyiel, Okugo and Jewi  including Pagak reception centre and local communities in Gambella to improve the living conditions and wellbeing of the population of concern. The problems against each output area with proposed interventions are presented below. Thus, the project will undertake establishment of permanent water supply system, construction of shared household latrines and camp wide hygiene promotion work. Gender and Protection mainstreaming will be an integral part of all the work.</narrative>
  </description>
